<!--Post: 9720--><!--Time: 1109616688-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9720"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 10:51 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I began to call this &#34;Where was BTK going with all of this?&#34;, but the simple answer would be: to finish his book and become a notorious serial killer, then disappear, maybe a taunting letter every few years just to keep everyone on their toes. When he was an aging, maladjusted loner living alone, able to slide in and out of town at will, that scenario worked. <BR> <BR>Now we find out that BTK has some serious baggage. <BR>A wife, three kids, fairly high profile job&#40;although no one seemed to miss him when he was out murdering people, and apparently staying out all night was no issue for his wife&#41;. <BR> <BR>On top of that was church, the zoning commission meetings, he probably had to show up at the city commission meetings also, and there were stray dogs and grass growing &#40;at least that explains why he had to take summers off from killing&#41;.  <BR> <BR>Apparently his ability to stop killing has been greatly exagerated and his methods and timing were getting sloppier all the time. Not only that, he starts drawing attention to himself and intentionally pissin the cops off to boot. Still, if it were just him, it would make some kind of sense in a BTKish sort of way. <BR> <BR>Supposing, he managed to bungle on through for a few more months and finish his book, was he planning on just sitting around and wait for the axe to fall? Was he planning on telling his wife, or was she about to have an &#39;unfortunate accident&#39;. <BR> <BR>Even then, how is he going to explain why, in his time of grief he leaves his job, church, friends, and the place he lived all his life to...do what? <BR> <BR>All of the shrinks say that BTK did NOT want to be caught. So how come the communications drops started to move toward Park City. He even&#39; allegedly, killed a woman a block away from his own house at one time.  <BR> <BR>His thinking would have made sense until a year ago. Everyone thought he was dead and gone, no one was connecting the murders to BTK and for some reason no one ever connected him to BTK&#40;he even managed to marry a woman who didn&#39;t question him about being out all night the night that Nancy Fox was murdered even though it was at the height of the &#34;BTK panic&#34;. If he had not resumed communication and just written the damn book he could have continued to live in BTK heaven and dropped the book somewhere when it was finished.  <BR> <BR>Last year, about this time, either something made Denny want &#40;or decide he was going&#41; to be caught, or kill himself. Either that, or there is a huge chunk of the story missing. I think the latter, as usual. <BR> <BR>What&#39;s missing? Maybe the urges got uncontrolable and he needed the notoriety to supplement his killing, maybe his wife found out, maybe he&#39;s been communicating all along, none of the new victms seem to be recent enough &#40;Tina Fredrick is not listed&#41;.  <BR> <BR>Does anyone know, or can you come up with a different scenario, than Denny planned to retire and move away in a few years and something derailed the plan about a year ago. Or can anyone figure out what happened to make him want to &#34;burn out, instead of rusting gracefully?&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9720-->
<!--Post: 9729--><!--Time: 1109620078-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9729"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 11:47 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In a psychological sense, when people get older there is a time in everyone&#39;s life where we all will question and review our accomplishments and failures, That is way some old people are bitter, because they didn&#39;t do anything they see as important with their lives, now it&#39;s to late. I believe this is part of what happened. He is a mean bitter person sounds like to most people anyway. This is what he did with his life, and now he wants everyone to know this is what he did. He has always thrived on attention, and taunting the police now was giving him that security he needed, to say hey this is what i have done with my life and I am feared and famous for it. i honestly dont believe he thought he would get caught, but I do believe he intended to make sure everyone knew it ws him before he died. and he would not have killed himself, but might have killed his family. I honestly to this day believe some of the members of his family were helping him. Just haven&#39;t figured out how or who yet.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9729-->
<!--Post: 9731--><!--Time: 1109620223-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9731"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 11:50 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTW reason:   If everyone knew him, then how come no one recognized him during the drops?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9731-->
<!--Post: 9748--><!--Time: 1109627163-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9748"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rev<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rev<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 1:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The theory that makes the most sense to me is this one: <BR> <BR>Dennis has been at his current job since 1990.  With the degree and the experience that he had working with ADT and as a code enforcer for the city, I&#39;m sure he figured he was worthy of being a &#34;real&#34; police officer.  Maybe sometime in 2003 or early 2004 he applied for a job as a &#34;real&#34; police officer and was turned down, or has been turned down repeatedly from 1990 to the present.  So he figures he&#39;ll taunt the biggest PD in the area, the Wichita PD, and prove how much smarter he is than them.  He couldn&#39;t very well taunt the Park City PD who possibly turned him down for the job, since most of his killings didn&#39;t occur there. <BR> <BR>I originally thought that maybe his wife or mother had died and that&#39;s what caused him to start communicating again, but that is not the case.  It&#39;ll be interesting to hear why he started up again. <BR> <BR>And Embersage, no one saw him make the cereal box drop in Park City, which is where everyone knew him.  No one would recognize him in Murdock Park making a drop, or anywhere else in Wichita for that matter.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9748-->
<!--Post: 9764--><!--Time: 1109632191-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9764"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Chiquitah<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Chiquitah<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 3:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I believe the particular drop E is referring to is the one where he made a drop off at the Home Depot and the security camera got him driving around over and over. Apparently checking to see if anyone had picked it up yet.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9764-->
<!--Post: 9817--><!--Time: 1109653823-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9817"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:williammichael@direcway.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 9:10 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I too admit being wrong about someone in his family dying or becoming ill as the trigger that made him come out of hiding. I thought either that or that his health had changed, but I will reserve judgement on that as we do not know for sure about his health.  I do not yet know what stressor brought him out of hiding. <BR>I do however firmly belive he never intended to get caught.  Why did he make dumb mistakes:  he got overconfident.  He thought he was invincible.  He was brilliat, everybody else was stupid.  He was so smooth butter felt rough by comparison.  He was so cool, chocolate would not melt in his mouth.  He was so fast, he could steal your belt at noon and your pants wouldn&#39;t fall until twelve-fifteen. <BR>At least that is what he thought. <BR>He got caught for two simple reasons:  everybody makes mistakes sometimes and if you play any game long enough, you will lose.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9817-->
<!--Post: 9837--><!--Time: 1109658105-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9837"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 10:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My big question on his &#34;Success strategy&#34; is this: <BR> <BR>Why, after successfully hiding for 31 years did he suddenly do something so stupid as to send an easily &#34;traceable&#34; floppy disk? <BR> <BR>Any moron knows that when you &#34;delete&#34; stuff on computers it is still there for any 2-bit computer nerd to find. You just can&#39;t easily see it yourself, unless you know how to &#34;dig&#34; on your computer. But how could he be IDIOTIC enough to send a disk that had HIS NAME &#40;or the name of his small church that he was &#34;President&#34; of&#41; on it?? Everyone says he was a real &#39;stickler&#39; for details, to the point of measuring how tall your blades of grass were on your lawn, etc. <BR> <BR>So how could he blow his cover so badly? Why didn&#39;t he just BUY A NEW, NON-TRACEABLE FLOPPY DISK to send to the cops?? <BR> <BR>DENNY, YOU DOPE! <BR> <BR>I guess we&#39;ll find out why &#40;hopefully&#41; at his wonderful trial.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9837-->
<!--Post: 9857--><!--Time: 1109663640-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9857"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 11:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think mention of Beattie&#39;s book -- as Rader perceived it -- forced his hand. It squares with his egotism and need for control and how dare someone write a book about him. Can&#39;t rule out AIDS or another terminal illness which may not be incapacitating for quite a time but I like the book idea most. Unfortunately we may never know. He may well say something if asked but sociopaths lie. Example: Bundy and Gacy, across the board, are thought to have killed more people than either is &#34;credited&#34; with; they were able, especially Bundy, to maintain a small amount of control by <i>not</i> mentioning where and possibly who these other victims were. I&#39;m sure each was asked if there were more victims and by saying &#34;no&#34; when the correct answer was probably &#34;yes,&#34; they still exerted control. I look forward to hearing from Rader but don&#39;t know how much can be believed. <BR> <BR>If the thread&#39;s title means how did he get away with it for thirty-one years, I&#39;d say: 1; the Otero attack was seen as a hit by LE 2; too many  people believed everything BTK wrote, especially early on 3; the attacks were spaced apart, LE had other things to do than solely muse about BTK, 4; serial killer information was almost non-existent in 1974, 5; very good luck, 6; knew how to blend in to a fare-thee-well, 7; internal WPD bad blood, then later the failure to share all information with other LE agencies, 8; police didn&#39;t release enough information to the public about him at the time, 9; organized serial killers are very hard to catch, esp. in 1974 Wichita. Numbers &#39;7&#39; and &#39;8&#39; are the biggest reasons.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9857-->
<!--Post: 9870--><!--Time: 1109667217-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9870"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 12:53 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It seems the BTK Strangler craved attention and recognition as a successful serial murderer. After the murder of Nancy Fox, the BTK Strangler was simply a serial murderer who was not apprehended. He did not have the infamy or brand awareness of Bundy, Berkowitz, Dahmer, Ramirez or Bittaker and Norris. He continued to murder in the 1980s and 1990s. The suspect did not admit it to avoid apprehension. At the end of the 1990s, the suspect most probably thought he was akin to the Zodiac Killer, the East Area Rapist, Jack the Ripper and Jack the Stripper, but lacked the attention. He demanded national and global attention as a serial murderer who not only derived gratification from murder, but from taunting the police, media and public. The suspect believed the police were incompetent and could taunt them with impunity. <BR> <BR>I strongly believe the prospect of Beattie publishing a book on his criminal career was the catalyst for him resuming communication in March 2004. The BTK Strangler was angered by Beattie having the temerity to scribe the narrative. The suspect believed Beattie was not accomplished and did not have the authority to write the narrative. The suspect believed Beattie would profit financially from the book and gain attention at his expense.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9870-->
<!--Post: 9940--><!--Time: 1109710672-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9940"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 12:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ivy - I resent the fact that your using the word &#34;successful&#34; in your ranting of Dennis Rader. Please find another word! There is nothing positive in the actions of this monster! As for the reason BTK reemerged, simply because two others were taking responsiblity for his work. Successful or unsuccesful! <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9940-->
<!--Post: 10008--><!--Time: 1109723650-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10008"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 4:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think George hit the bullseye. Beattie&#39;s book was the &#34;event&#34; I was looking for. Rayder&#39;s plan was apparently on track until he felt his story was being hijacked. <BR> <BR>It brings to mind another string where we were going around about pissin off &#34;BTK the artist&#34;. I guess that was the ticket to tripping him up after all. <BR> <BR>It takes a big man to admit when he&#39;s wrong. If I see one I&#39;ll let have him get back to you.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10008-->
<!--Post: 10039--><!--Time: 1109734033-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10039"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 7:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rocky, <BR> <BR>You are entitled to resent the term &#39;successful serial murderer.&#39; The expression was used to describe the psychology of the BTK Strangler. I was not praising him.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
